{
  "description": "Request rules every helper shares, decided by the shared core (ADR-DESK-054): a focused field read's bound (1 to 20,000 UTF-16 units) and its reply (null when longer, else redacted), and a paste's text (not empty, at most 512 KiB, no NUL) and deadline (later than now, at most 5 s ahead), the clipboard a paste saves and puts back (500 ms after the paste keys; at most 64 MiB and 256 formats), and a microphone start's or stop's session (a whole number from 1) and a start's recording rate (whole hertz, 8,000 to 96,000), and a screen read's number (a whole number from 1; a read may have none, a stop may not). Each helper's suite runs every case through the C ABI it ships with; `refused: true` cases are refused.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a field bound at the most a request may ask",
      "request": {
        "field": {
          "maxLength": 20000
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "maxLength": 20000
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a field bound of one unit",
      "request": {
        "field": {
          "maxLength": 1
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "maxLength": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "no text read from the field",
      "request": {
        "field": {
          "maxLength": 20000,
          "text": null
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "value": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a field's text, its secret-looking part taken out",
      "request": {
        "field": {
          "maxLength": 20000,
          "text": "Draft reply. password: hunter2x"
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "value": "Draft reply. password: [redacted]"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a rich editor's text, its block breaks as the line breaks they are",
      "request": {
        "field": {
          "maxLength": 20000,
          "text": "Hi All,\nWhy does it move?\n\n--"
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "value": "Hi All,\nWhy does it move?\n\n--"
      }
    },
    {
